Hi Flipper team — I've been building an autonomous cognitive runtime framework (AEGENTIS) and a sovereign security stack across Windows, embedded Linux, and XR environments. I'm exploring how to contribute to Flipper One and wanted to check appetite before drafting anything formal.

Two specific angles I'm considering:

1. **Testing sub-project**: A self-healing diagnostic framework that auto-detects and resolves hardware subsystem failures, plus a cryptographically-verified success logging protocol for permanent audit trails. Think of it as moving from static test scripts to an autonomous validation layer.

2. **Linux (CPU Software) sub-project**: A lightweight distributed mesh runtime for device-to-device cognitive routing on Rockchip Linux, plus containerized LLM inference tooling (Groq API bridge) and deterministic build-deploy pipelines.

Both are derived from real operational systems already running on my hardware (ROG Ally X, Meta Quest 3, Android automotive). Before I write any code or open issues, I wanted to ask: are there active maintainers in Testing or Linux who'd be open to an architecture discussion? Or should I start somewhere else in the stack?

Happy to share a one-page architecture doc if anyone wants to see scope before I commit to a full PR.

